  "notes": "Two MSSVs (2-MS-249, 2-MS-251) independently failed as-found acceptance criteria on the same surveillance test date, modeled as two parallel FailureMode nodes fed by the same two root causes (vibration effect on test instrumentation, and setpoint drift) per rule 5. No BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted: ADVs and other MSSVs are discussed only as design/safety-analysis bounding context (FSAR Ch.14), not as stated-operable backups during the inoperability window itself. SPVD/LVDT modeled as Component since it is a specific test-measurement device implicated directly in the failure mechanism, not a system. Cause code B (Design/Manufacturing/Installation) taken verbatim from Block 13/cause_code field, though narrative reads as a mixed vibration/drift phenomenon; theme captures this nuance without overriding the official code per rule 4."
